  "recipeCuisine": "Malaysia",
  "name": "Singapore Egg Noodles",
  "text": "Singapore Egg Noodles\n\nYield: 4\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nIngredients\n\n3 cloves of garlic (finely chopped),\n\n115 g pork fillet (cut into thin strips),\n\n115 g fresh fish fillet (cut into bitesize pieces),\n\n115 g fresh prawns (shelled and deveined),\n\n2 small squid (cleaned and sliced reserving tenticles),\n\n300 ml chicken stock,\n\n450 g egg noodles,\n\n1 carrot (shredded),\n\n2 tbsp dark soy sauce,\n\n2 tbsp light soy sauce,\n\nGround black pepper,\n\nSmall bunch of fresh coriander (roughly chopped).\n\nPreparation\n\n1. In a wok fry off the garlic.\n\n2. When it becomes fragrant stir in the pork, fish, prawns,  and squid, tossing them around in the pan for 1 minute.\n\n3. Pour in the stock and simmer to reduce it.\n\n4. Add the noodles and toss them around in the wok for 1 minute.\n\n5. Stir in the carrot and cabbage.\n\n6. Add the soy sauces and cook until most of the liquid has been evaporated.\n\n7. Season with pepper.",
  "recipeYield": "4",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "3 cloves of garlic (finely chopped),",
    "115 g pork fillet (cut into thin strips),",
    "115 g fresh fish fillet (cut into bitesize pieces),",
    "115 g fresh prawns (shelled and deveined),",
    "2 small squid (cleaned and sliced reserving tenticles),",
    "300 ml chicken stock,",
    "450 g egg noodles,",
    "1 carrot (shredded),",
    "2 tbsp dark soy sauce,",
    "2 tbsp light soy sauce,",
    "Ground black pepper,",
    "Small bunch of fresh coriander (roughly chopped)."
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "In a wok fry off the garlic."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "When it becomes fragrant stir in the pork, fish, prawns,  and squid, tossing them around in the pan for 1 minute."
    },
